---
/*
  flying.astro — the flight training page.

  Kept as its own page rather than folded into About, because the training is
  the most distinctive thing on the site and it is where the flagship project
  came from.
*/
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
import Figure from "../components/Figure.astro";
import { milestones, statusLabel } from "../data/flying";
---

<Layout
  title="Flying"
  description="Student pilot training toward an FAA Private Pilot Certificate in Cessna 172s, and how it connects to the embedded work."
>
  <PageHeader
    title="Flying"
    lead="Student pilot working toward an FAA Private Pilot Certificate, Airplane Single Engine Land."
  />

  <div class="container body">
    <div class="body__figure">
      <Figure slot="flying-cockpit" loading="eager" />
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Where I train</h2>
      <p>
        I fly Cessna 172s at Triad Aviation Academy at KGSO in Greensboro, North
        Carolina. I have logged over 70 hours, including solo cross country and
        night flights, and I completed ground school through Sporty's.
      </p>

      <h2>What I am comfortable with</h2>
      <p>
        Most of my cross country planning has been around KGSO, KTTA, and KMWK.
        I am comfortable requesting and working under VFR flight following,
        handling ATC radio work, navigating with the GNS 430, identifying VOR
        and NDB stations, and flying the 172 by its published V speeds.
      </p>

      <h2>Why it belongs on an engineering site</h2>
      <p>
        Flying is the reason the Aviation Weather Display exists. I check METARs
        before I fly, and wanting that information on a screen on my desk rather
        than inside an app is what turned into an embedded project.
      </p>
      <p>
        It has also changed how I work. A preflight is a checklist you run the
        same way every time precisely because you will eventually be tired, or
        rushed, or certain you already checked. Aviation assumes people make
        mistakes and builds the procedure around that assumption instead of
        around good intentions. That is a better model for engineering than
        trusting yourself to be careful.
      </p>

      <h2>Where I am now</h2>
      <p>
        The FAA written exam is the next milestone, and it is what I am studying
        for. Training has been paused while I have been at school.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="milestones" aria-labelledby="milestones-heading">
      <h2 id="milestones-heading" class="milestones__heading">Training so far</h2>
      <ul class="milestones__list">
        {
          milestones.map((milestone) => (
            <li class:list={["milestone", `milestone--${milestone.status}`]}>
              <span class="milestone__dot" aria-hidden="true" />
              <span class="milestone__label">{milestone.label}</span>
              <span class="milestone__status">{statusLabel[milestone.status]}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .body {
    padding-block: var(--space-5) var(--space-6);
  }

  .body__figure {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-5);
  }

  .milestones {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    padding-top: var(--space-5);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .milestones__heading {
    font-size: var(--fs-lg);
  }

  .milestones__list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: var(--space-4) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    max-width: 520px;
  }

  .milestone {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-3);
    padding-block: var(--space-2);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .milestone:last-child {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }

  .milestone__dot {
    width: 7px;
    height: 7px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    background: var(--border-strong);
  }

  .milestone--complete .milestone__dot {
    background: var(--status-done);
  }

  .milestone--current .milestone__dot {
    background: var(--accent);
  }

  .milestone__label {
    flex: 1;
  }

  /* The word carries the meaning, so the dot colour is reinforcement only. */
  .milestone__status {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--fs-xs);
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }
</style>
